  "operatorNotes": {
    "anthropic": "The $10.00 cache-write ceiling covers the more expensive published one-hour cache-write rate, not the five-minute one.",
    "openai": "Cache write is a separately published rate.",
    "google": "Google does not publish a separate implicit-cache creation charge. The $2.00 figure here is deliberately the full uncached-input rate, so that a cache miss cannot exceed the reserved input cost. It is NOT a separately published cache-write tariff.",
    "sources": [
      "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching",
      "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.6-sol",
      "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing",
      "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/gemini-3"
    ],
    "addresses": "Origins only. Each adapter appends its own complete path — /v1/messages, /v1/responses, /v1beta/models — so a baseUrl that also carries /v1 sends the request to /v1/v1/... That is what the first paid canary's 404 was.",
    "google_output_ceiling": "8192, not the 4096 the other two carry, and it is a measured number. This model's thinking is billed inside its output, so an output ceiling is a ceiling on thinking AND answer together: the first critic call this canary ever got past a 400 spent 27.8 s and stopped at 4096 with the envelope unfinished — output_ceiling_reached, a whole paid attempt for no reading. It stays inside the per-attempt worst case the authority is sized from: 8192 in at $2.00 plus 8192 out at $12.00 is $0.114, under the $0.18432 an attempt may hold, so nothing about the authority changes."
  },
